lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen.pm:326-327:

  elsif ($type eq "number") {
      return "Str";  # Treat numbers as strings for now

A JSON number in a generated class round-trips as a quoted string:
{"cpu": 1.5} comes back out as {"cpu": "1.5"}. The API server rejects
that for a numeric field. "for now" has outlived whatever now it meant.

Blocked on the same gap as karr #66: the k8s DSL has no numeric scalar
type to map onto. Int exists and int-casts in TO_JSON; there is no Num.
So the fix is a DSL addition (a Num form plus its TO_JSON branch,
mirroring is_int) and only then the AutoGen mapping.

Note the difference to Quantity (karr #52): Quantity is a *string* type
upstream and correctly stays a string. This ticket is about schemas that
genuinely declare type: number.

Found by the autogen lane while implementing karr #55-#57/#60 (verified
by the orchestrating agent).
